      "risk_review": {
        "status": "complete",
        "reviewer": "alpha-batch-54",
        "notes": "Independently reviewed Definition and Verification 1.1–2.1 against all six direct supplier statements and Arora et al. §2 Definitions 1–2 (PDF p.3). The least-index maximizer has strict comparisons against smaller labels and weak comparisons against larger labels; finite nonempty K>=2 makes the maximum and competing maximum defined. Differences and finite maxima are measurable; finite singleton fibers and finite label slices establish classifier, margin and error-event measurability. The measurable F and finite-discrete selector specify sample dependence; decoders, helper and codebook are fixed. q=0 gives one empty code; r=1, tied scores and repeated decoders are allowed. m>=1 and epsilon>0 are explicit; empty comparison intersections are X. Supplied finite objects require no AC. No diagrams or interrupted definition links occur. No defect or unmet prerequisite found."
