          "claim": "On a sample satisfying the compression condition, if $M_{f_S}(X_i,Y_i)>2\\epsilon$, then for each $j\\ne Y_i$ the coordinatewise distortion bound [F3] gives $g_{s,\\alpha(S)}(X_i)_{Y_i}-g_{s,\\alpha(S)}(X_i)_j\\ge f_S(X_i)_{Y_i}-f_S(X_i)_j-2\\epsilon\\ge M_{f_S}(X_i,Y_i)-2\\epsilon>0$. Thus the decoded classifier predicts $Y_i$ at that observation. Each decoded training-error indicator is therefore at most $\\mathbf1\\{M_{f_S}(X_i,Y_i)\\le2\\epsilon\\}$, and averaging gives $\\widehat R_S(h_{s,\\alpha(S)})\\le\\widehat L_{2\\epsilon}(f_S;S)$.",
