        {
          "id": "derivation-2.1",
          "step": "2.1",
          "claim": "Fix $a\\in\\mathcal A$, write $Z_i=(X_i,Y_i)$ and $U_i=\\ell_a(Z_i)$, and put $\\mu=R_P(h_{s,a})=\\int\\ell_a\\,dP$ by [F23]. Each $Z_i$ has law $P$ by [F7] and [F17], so [F18] gives $\\mathbb E U_i=\\mu$. The $U_i$ are independent by [F12], since $\\ell_a$ is measurable by step 1.1. The function $x\\mapsto\\lambda(x-\\mu)$ is continuous by [F20], and [F16] and [F21] make $g_\\lambda(x):=\\exp(\\lambda(x-\\mu))$ continuous. Its preimage of every open set is open; preimages preserve complements and countable unions, so [F22] makes preimages of all Borel sets Borel by [F9]. Thus $g_\\lambda$ is a nonnegative Borel function.",
          "inputs": [
