          "claim": "By finite-product factorization [F13], exponential addition [F15], and the bounded-variable MGF estimate [F11], $\\mathbb E\\exp\\!\\left(\\lambda\\sum_{i=1}^m(U_i-\\mu)\\right)=\\prod_{i=1}^m\\mathbb E\\exp(\\lambda(U_i-\\mu))\\le\\exp(m\\lambda^2/8)$ for every real $\\lambda$. This finite MGF argument uses no choice principle by [A1].",
