      "risk_review": {
        "status": "complete",
        "reviewer": "alpha-batch-54",
        "notes": "Independently read all seven proof steps, 23 direct supplier statements, the complete Hoeffding MGF proof and its actual linearity supplier, reader finding and native refute-54 report. Measurability follows from rectangle preimages, finite selector fibers, finite label slices and arithmetic; no uncountable supremum is used. Pairwise score error is at most 2epsilon; only margins strictly above that value force correct decoding. Fixed-code Bernoulli losses are IID, have expectation equal to population error, and nonnegative Borel exponential transforms satisfy factorization and the unit-interval MGF bound. lambda=-4t reverses the lower-deviation comparison and Markov gives exp(-2mt^2). r^q/delta>1 proves tau>0 even at q=0 or r=1; union over at most r^q codes and intersection with a full-measure compression event allow the data-dependent selector. The finite codebook/selector are given; no AC is used. The conclusion concerns only compressed risk, not original risk or existence of a network compressor. Arora et al. §2 and Appendix A.1 were checked; the local strict 2epsilon correction is necessary. Published Hoeffding F1/2.1/5.1 has a nonfatal missing explicit linearity citation, closed only as nonfatal-recorded with owner maintenance pending; its declared cor-expectation-linearity-monotonicity-and-modulus-bound Statement 1 immediately supplies both uses. No mathematical blocker, diagram defect or statement-link interruption."
